# markdown-syntax AST->HTML conformance suite v1: syntax decisions
source: wikilinks
decision: Wiki links: the title follows the pipe, and a wiki link wins over link and reference syntax.
count: 15

--- case 1 options allow_dangerous_html,allow_dangerous_protocol label-bytes 150 input-bytes 27 expected-bytes 109
from commonmark/commonmark.cases #548; decision 0007: `[[…]]` is a wiki link, its title follows the pipe, and it wins over a defined reference label
--- input
[[[foo]]]

[[[foo]]]: /url

--- expected
<p>[<a href="foo" data-wikilink="true">foo</a>]</p>
<p>[<a href="foo" data-wikilink="true">foo</a>]: /url</p>
--- end
--- case 2 options allow_dangerous_html,allow_dangerous_protocol label-bytes 150 input-bytes 41 expected-bytes 63
from commonmark/commonmark.cases #559; decision 0007: `[[…]]` is a wiki link, its title follows the pipe, and it wins over a defined reference label
--- input
[[*foo* bar]]

[*foo* bar]: /url "title"

--- expected
<p><a href="*foo*%20bar" data-wikilink="true">*foo* bar</a></p>
--- end
